The risks from my earlier report still apply, and I changed none of them:
- Tabs to the right of a closed one now remount.
- A new tab can reuse a key that was used before.
- Old `?tabs=t1,t3` URLs are not normalised on load.
- Callers outside this module must remap any active key themselves.
- The README example `?tabs=t1,t3` is stale.
- The other four PRECEDENT.md files don't reference `§stable-tab-keys`.
